<title>HONG KONG: Taiwan's ProMOS Technologies sets US$320 mln loan.</title>
<headline>Taiwan's ProMOS Technologies sets US$320 mln loan.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following syndicated loan facility was announced by arranger BA Asia.</p>
<p>The borrower is a joint venture between Mosel Vitelic Inc and Siemens AG to produce advanced dynamic random access memory, or DRAM, chips in Taiwan.</p>
<p>The loan will be secured by a letter of undertaking from Mosel, an off-take agreement from Mosel and Siemens, mortgage on equipment and a negative pledge of shares.</p>
<p>Details are as follows:</p>
<p> BORROWER   PROMOS TECHNOLOGIES INC</p>
<p> AMOUNT     US$320 MLN    TYPE	TERM LOAN</p>
<p> MARGIN     L+52.5BP	MATURITY  7 YRS     AVGE LIFE  4.5 YRS</p>
<p> PUTS	 NONE	    CALLS     NONE	REPLIES  MID-APRIL</p>
<p> DRAWDOWN   --		AVAIL     21 MTHS</p>
<p>REPAYMENT  11 SEMI-ANNUAL EQUAL INSTALMENTS AFTER 2 YRS GRACE ARRANGERS  BA ASIA (COORDINATING), WESTDEUTSCHE LANDESBANK AND</p>
<p>		SUMITOMO BANK</p>
<p> CO-ARRANGERS   DEVELOPMENT BANK OF SINGAPORE, FUJI BANK,</p>
<p>		    BAYERISCHE LANDESBANK, ROYAL BANK OF CANADA AND</p>
<p>		    INTERNATIONAL COMMERCIAL BANK OF CHINA.</p>
<p>MGT LEVELS AND FEES</p>
<p>   COMMITMENT FEE    20BP</p>
<p>   SENIOR MANAGERS   US$15 MLN+   10.0 BP   ALL-IN  54.72</p>
<p>   MANAGERS	    US$10 MLN+    7.5 BP   ALL-IN  54.16</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6960</p>
